# Kernel ASM / locking — playbook is law

This repo follows the **Production-Grade x86 Context Switch + Locking Playbook**.
Anything that conflicts is wrong and must be rewritten. No soft/compiler atomics
as the locking source of truth. **CPU-level only** (`LOCK` / implicit-LOCK `XCHG`,
`PAUSE`, `CMPXCHG`, `XADD`, `FXSAVE`/`XSAVE`, CR3-if-changed).

Current tree may still assemble as i686 (`elf32`); semantics must match the
playbook. x86-64 register names in the playbook map to the 32-bit callee-saved
set on i386 until the arch migrates. Do **not** invent parallel “compat”
locking paths.

## Hard bans

- `__sync_*`, `__atomic_*`, C `volatile` CAS loops as the **implementation** of
  kernel spinlocks (wrappers may call asm; the atomicity lives in asm).
- Spin loops **without** `pause`.
- Context switch that skips FPU/SIMD state when the compiler may use XMM.
- Unconditional `mov cr3` when old CR3 == new CR3 (full TLB flush tax).
- Claiming “atomic” without `LOCK` / implicit-LOCK `XCHG` / aligned single-word
  store under x86 TSO (document which).
- Mixing cdecl (i386) with SysV AMD64 arg regs in the same asm ABI.

## Context switch contract

- Name: `context_switch_locked(old_ctx, new_ctx)` — caller holds runqueue lock +
  IRQs off. The switch function does **not** take locks.
- Saves callee-saved GPRs into `cpu_context_t`, swaps stack via saved SP.
- Saves/restores FPU via `FXSAVE`/`FXRSTOR` (or `XSAVE`/`XRSTOR` when mask ready)
  through `fpu_area*` (16B+ aligned, ≥512B).
- Reads CR3 into old; writes new CR3 **only if different**.
- After stack switch: update TSS ESP0/RSP0 before returning to user (if ring3).
- Count every push/pop and document offsets in comments. Never “probably right”.

## Spinlock contract

```text
acquire: xchg(1) → if was 0 ok; else pause + load-test until 0, retry xchg
release: aligned store 0  (x86 TSO = store-release; no LOCK needed on x86)
```

- Short critical sections only; never sleep while holding.
- IRQ handlers: `cli` + spin (`irqsave`) or deadlock on same CPU.
- Nested locks: document lock order; never AB-BA.
- Prefer ticket lock when fairness across many cores matters.

## Atomics

- `lock inc` / `lock xadd` / `lock cmpxchg` in asm (or equivalent single insn).
- RMW without `LOCK` is not SMP-safe.

## AI output rules (every asm change)

1. Hand-count stack/offsets; show math in comments.
2. Never skip FPU/SIMD in switch.
3. CR3 write only when changed (PCID later).
4. State IRQ/lock precondition in the symbol name or a one-line contract comment.
5. Prove atomics (`LOCK` / `XCHG`).
6. Always `pause` in spin wait.
7. Treat new kernel asm as **reference until tested** — silent corruption is the failure mode.

## OS thread vs HW thread

- `process_t` / `cpu_context_t` = OS thread private state.
- `cpu_t` = HW logical CPU (core/SMT). Scheduler maps OS threads onto logical CPUs.
